  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 148 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nAn upper level wave and saturation aloft will move through the area \nlater this afternoon through tonight. While some very weak \ninstability is expected aloft, thunder is very unlikely. Saturation \naloft is most prominent between I-90 and the Missouri River and with \nthe dry layer in the low levels not excessively dry, some quarter to \npossibly half inch rainfall amounts are possible over about a 6 hour \nperiod.\n\nFriday should generally be dry and mild, maybe a few showers in \nnorthwest IA during the morning. Highs remain below normal, but will \nbe a bit higher with most locations climbing into the 80s, coolest \nin northwest IA.\n\nHot conditions return for the weekend into early next week. The\nlatest bias corrected data is running about 5 degrees cooler \nthan the model output for Saturday through Monday. Will have to \nkeep an eye on trends as the heat approaches as last weeks warm \nup the NBM overdid the heat almost every day. This time around \nthere will be a better potential for southwest winds at the \nsurface which generally aids in heating out, so maybe the 3-6 \ndegree warm bias that was seen with the past warm up will be a \nlittle less. Long story short, the bias corrected output falls \njust short of a heat advisory both Saturday and Sunday while the\nNBM is basically in heat advisory both days.\n\nConvective chances are pretty small through Monday. A slightly \nstronger wave will drop south on Sunday and bring a small threat for \nsevere storms. The better chance should be north and east of the \narea. This will be the main time frame to track over the\nupcoming days.\n\nTuesday through Thursday should see upper level ridging just west of \nthe area with stronger northwest flow aloft just northeast of the \narea. This leaves the area in position for above normal \ntemperatures, but possibly not on the excessive side as weak waves \nwill at times allow slightly cooler air to move in. With these weak \nwaves will come periodic chance for showers and thunderstorms but \nfor now confidence in this activity is low.",
